{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AW42svVy9rJh7ssLDwZWtf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 2026-08-30 — WI-538: arm the complexity sensor here, re-base the module-size ratchet to SLOC (OI-68 phase 2, ruled 1c)\n2\t\n3\t**Summary.** Executes phase 2 of the OI-68 complexity-sensor program at the shape\n4\tthe owner ruled on 2026-08-30 — **1c / 2a / 3a / 4a**, NOT the driver's recommended\n5\t1a. The ruling is on record in `docs/requirements/open-items.toml`\n6\t`[open_item.OI-68]` (`status = \"ruled\"`). Because it landed 1c, phase 2 is\n7\t**arm + re-base**, never arm + retire: both sensors stay armed, nothing is\n8\tdeleted, no pointer moves.\n9\t\n10\tThree acts, in one direction:\n11\t\n12\t1. **Arm (3a).** A new `[step:complexity]` in `docs/stack.ini`\n13\t   (`layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) runs\n14\t   `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` — the exact-equality compare, in\n15\t   both directions, nonzero on either. SR-183 already carries both postures in one\n16\t   row (\"gated only where a repo opts in\"), so arming mints NO new spine row; the\n17\t   opt-in is the step's presence in `docs/stack.ini`. Report-only stays the\n18\t   shipped default (that ships in phase 3, a separate WI).\n19\t\n20\t2. **Scope (2a).** The sensor's census surface widens to `tests/` as well as\n21\t   `project-trajectory/scripts/` — `DEFAULT_INCLUDE` in `check_complexity.py`, the\n22\t   single home of this repo's census surface — and `docs/complexity-baseline` is\n23\t   re-stamped to seed the ~20 `tests/` functions over the threshold. The line\n24\t   ratchet stays scripts-only, per the ruling.\n25\t\n26\t3. **Re-base (1c).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` is re-based from raw\n27\t   physical lines (`len(text.splitlines())`) to **SLOC** — non-blank, non-comment,\n28\t   non-docstring — the definition held once beside the sensor\n29\t   (`check_complexity.module_sloc`) and imported by the ratchet, so the two sensors\n30\t   share one definition of a source line. `THRESHOLD` re-based 1500 → **1000 SLOC**\n31\t   and the `BASELINE` dict fully re-stamped to SLOC values (derivation below).\n32\t   Nothing deleted: the file, its `[generated]` `linecounts` row, its\n33\t   `OTHERWISE_ENFORCED` entry, and WI-521's debt-owner pointer all stay.\n34\t\n35\t**Threshold derivation (1500 raw → 1000 SLOC).** Measured at this branch's base\n36\tover `project-trajectory/scripts/`: the 9 modules the raw-1500 ratchet baselined\n37\tscore 1081–3364 SLOC (`intake.py` the smallest member at 1081); the largest\n38\tNON-member is `traj_panels.py` at 891 SLOC. A SLOC threshold anywhere in 900–1000\n39\tpreserves EXACTLY those 9 modules — a 190-line clean gap — so 1000 is the round\n40\tchoice that re-stamps the current watch set onto the code axis without deleting an\n41\tentry or admitting a new one. This is the \"one-time full re-stamp with the\n42\tderivation on record\" the ruling names.\n43\t\n44\t**Not touched, deliberately.** OI-68 is already flipped `ruled` (done at the\n45\tsitting), so no `open-items.toml` edit and no `gen_open_items` regen. The\n46\t`linecounts` freshness-wiring kind is left as-is — it is an internal join key and\n47\tSLOC is still a source-line count; the axis definition lives in the ratchet's own\n48\tdocstring. `test_import_layers.py` / `test_agent_loop.py` docstring references to\n49\tthe ratchet stay valid (the file stays); only `traj_context.py`'s pinned\n50\t\"1,500-line threshold\" is generalised, since that number is now stale.\n51\t\n52\tDeferred open items: none — the ruling (OI-68) is on record and this phase\n53\texecutes it; it files no new question.\n54\t\n55\t**Rework (REVIEW-A, MINOR, addressed 2026-08-30).** The review found the ratchet's\n56\tre-based module docstring still asserted the two sensors \"cover the same files …\n57\tand differ only in what they measure\" — false once 2a widened the complexity\n58\tsensor's `DEFAULT_INCLUDE` to `tests/` while this ratchet stayed scripts-only\n59\t(`conftest.SCRIPTS`). Corrected the docstring to state that the shared\n60\t`check_complexity.module_sloc` source-line definition is the ONLY axis the two\n61\tsensors hold in common: they diverge in BOTH what they measure (module SIZE vs\n62\tfunction COMPLEXITY) AND which files they cover (kit scripts only vs scripts +\n63\t`tests/`). Docstring-only; no predicate moved, ratchet + complexity tests still\n64\tgreen.\n65\t\n66\t**Verification.**\n67\t\n68\t- **Arming (3a).** `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` →\n69\t  `OK - 200 row(s) over 15, unchanged from baseline.`, exit 0.\n70\t- **Re-base units (1c/2a).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` +\n71\t  `tests/test_check_complexity.py` → 50 passed.\n72\t- **Commit bar.** `pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` → 1427 passed, 6 skipped (43.9s);\n73\t  `check_smoke_budget.py --mode enforce` → 38.1s vs 60s budget, within, exit 0.\n74\t- **Full unfiltered suite — GREEN, run in three disjoint file-partition batches**\n75\t  (the box was loaded past the 10-min single-shot timeout — the two prior resume\n76\t  sessions, iteration logs 003/004, were each reaped mid-single-shot-run with the\n77\t  background suite killed on teardown, which is why this row stayed open; the\n78\t  batched form is the standing fallback for that): fast in-process modules (74)\n79\t  1427 passed / 6 skipped; slow subprocess/scaffold modules split 35 + 36 → 907\n80\t  passed / 2 skipped and 857 passed / 8 skipped. **Union: all 145 test files, each\n81\t  run exactly once — 3191 passed, 16 skipped, 0 failed.**\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"637a71a5-9338-491f-a894-a25ca0d25af8","uuid":"4f60fda1-7fa3-47aa-9035-c9291dc20725","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:56:34.684Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi-538-arm-and-rebase\\docs\\log.d\\2026-08-30-wi538-arm-and-rebase.md","content":"## 2026-08-30 — WI-538: arm the complexity sensor here, re-base the module-size ratchet to SLOC (OI-68 phase 2, ruled 1c)\n\n**Summary.** Executes phase 2 of the OI-68 complexity-sensor program at the shape\nthe owner ruled on 2026-08-30 — **1c / 2a / 3a / 4a**, NOT the driver's recommended\n1a. The ruling is on record in `docs/requirements/open-items.toml`\n`[open_item.OI-68]` (`status = \"ruled\"`). Because it landed 1c, phase 2 is\n**arm + re-base**, never arm + retire: both sensors stay armed, nothing is\ndeleted, no pointer moves.\n\nThree acts, in one direction:\n\n1. **Arm (3a).** A new `[step:complexity]` in `docs/stack.ini`\n   (`layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) runs\n   `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` — the exact-equality compare, in\n   both directions, nonzero on either. SR-183 already carries both postures in one\n   row (\"gated only where a repo opts in\"), so arming mints NO new spine row; the\n   opt-in is the step's presence in `docs/stack.ini`. Report-only stays the\n   shipped default (that ships in phase 3, a separate WI).\n\n2. **Scope (2a).** The sensor's census surface widens to `tests/` as well as\n   `project-trajectory/scripts/` — `DEFAULT_INCLUDE` in `check_complexity.py`, the\n   single home of this repo's census surface — and `docs/complexity-baseline` is\n   re-stamped to seed the ~20 `tests/` functions over the threshold. The line\n   ratchet stays scripts-only, per the ruling.\n\n3. **Re-base (1c).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` is re-based from raw\n   physical lines (`len(text.splitlines())`) to **SLOC** — non-blank, non-comment,\n   non-docstring — the definition held once beside the sensor\n   (`check_complexity.module_sloc`) and imported by the ratchet, so the two sensors\n   share one definition of a source line. `THRESHOLD` re-based 1500 → **1000 SLOC**\n   and the `BASELINE` dict fully re-stamped to SLOC values (derivation below).\n   Nothing deleted: the file, its `[generated]` `linecounts` row, its\n   `OTHERWISE_ENFORCED` entry, and WI-521's debt-owner pointer all stay.\n\n**Threshold derivation (1500 raw → 1000 SLOC).** Measured at this branch's base\nover `project-trajectory/scripts/`: the 9 modules the raw-1500 ratchet baselined\nscore 1081–3364 SLOC (`intake.py` the smallest member at 1081); the largest\nNON-member is `traj_panels.py` at 891 SLOC. A SLOC threshold anywhere in 900–1000\npreserves EXACTLY those 9 modules — a 190-line clean gap — so 1000 is the round\nchoice that re-stamps the current watch set onto the code axis without deleting an\nentry or admitting a new one. This is the \"one-time full re-stamp with the\nderivation on record\" the ruling names.\n\n**Not touched, deliberately.** OI-68 is already flipped `ruled` (done at the\nsitting), so no `open-items.toml` edit and no `gen_open_items` regen. The\n`linecounts` freshness-wiring kind is left as-is — it is an internal join key and\nSLOC is still a source-line count; the axis definition lives in the ratchet's own\ndocstring. `test_import_layers.py` / `test_agent_loop.py` docstring references to\nthe ratchet stay valid (the file stays); only `traj_context.py`'s pinned\n\"1,500-line threshold\" is generalised, since that number is now stale.\n\nDeferred open items: none — the ruling (OI-68) is on record and this phase\nexecutes it; it files no new question.\n\n**Rework (REVIEW-A, MINOR, addressed 2026-08-30).** The review found the ratchet's\nre-based module docstring still asserted the two sensors \"cover the same files …\nand differ only in what they measure\" — false once 2a widened the complexity\nsensor's `DEFAULT_INCLUDE` to `tests/` while this ratchet stayed scripts-only\n(`conftest.SCRIPTS`). Corrected the docstring to state that the shared\n`check_complexity.module_sloc` source-line definition is the ONLY axis the two\nsensors hold in common: they diverge in BOTH what they measure (module SIZE vs\nfunction COMPLEXITY) AND which files they cover (kit scripts only vs scripts +\n`tests/`). Docstring-only; no predicate moved, ratchet + complexity tests still\ngreen.\n\n**Verification.**\n\n- **Arming (3a).** `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` →\n  `OK - 200 row(s) over 15, unchanged from baseline.`, exit 0.\n- **Re-base units (1c/2a).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` +\n  `tests/test_check_complexity.py` → 50 passed.\n- **Commit bar.** `pytest -q -n auto -m smoke` → 1427 passed, 6 skipped (43.9s);\n  `check_smoke_budget.py --mode enforce` → 38.1s vs 60s budget, within, exit 0.\n- **Full unfiltered suite — GREEN, run in three disjoint file-partition batches**\n  (the box was loaded past the 10-min single-shot timeout — the two prior resume\n  sessions, iteration logs 003/004, were each reaped mid-single-shot-run with the\n  background suite killed on teardown, which is why this row stayed open; the\n  batched form is the standing fallback for that): fast in-process modules (74)\n  1427 passed / 6 skipped; slow subprocess/scaffold modules split 35 + 36 → 907\n  passed / 2 skipped and 857 passed / 8 skipped. **Union: all 145 test files, each\n  run exactly once — 3191 passed, 16 skipped, 0 failed.**\n","numLines":82,"startLine":1,"totalLines":82}}}
